        0,
        "subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is character 1, shown in <Video 1>.\n<Audio 1> is the voice-timbre reference for <Subject 1> (S1).\n<Subject 2> is character 2, shown in <Video 2>.\n<Audio 2> is the voice-timbre reference for <Subject 2> (S2).\n\nsummary:\n[reference generation + audio reference] A quiet conversation with new dialogue.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Audio 1>: reference - retain vocal identity while generating the new words.\n<Audio 2>: reference - retain vocal identity while generating the new words.\n\ndetailed_description:\n[Shot 1] A stationary eye-level camera frames the characters side by side in a quiet room under soft daylight. Their individual reference appearances remain consistent. They speak one at a time; the others listen with closed mouths.\nBetween 0.5 and 2.5 seconds, <Subject 1> (S1) says <d>[English] The old bridge is still standing.</d> with calm, natural delivery, then closes their mouth.\nBetween 3.0 and 5.0 seconds, <Subject 2> (S2) says <d>[English] Then we can cross before sunset.</d> with calm, natural delivery, then closes their mouth.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nQuiet room ambience below the dialogue.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nN/A",
        "1,0.5,2.5\n2,3.0,5.0",
        "native",
